      "category": "verbosity_fingerprint",
      "check_type": "length_range",
      "passed": false,
      "errored": false,
      "error": null,
      "latency_ms": 5343.3,
      "prompt_tokens": 25,
      "completion_tokens": 1064,
      "output": "\n\nWater is a chemical substance composed of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom, forming the molecule **H₂O**. It is one of the most essential and abundant substances on Earth, playing a critical role in sustaining life and shaping the planet's environment. Here's a breakdown of its key characteristics:\n\n### **Chemical Composition**\n- **Molecular Structure**: Water is a polar molecule, with oxygen (more electronegative) pulling electrons toward itself, creating a slight negative charge on the oxygen end and positive charges on the hydrogen ends. This polarity leads to **hydrogen bonding**, which gives water many of its unique properties.\n\n### **Physical Properties**\n- **States of Matter**: Water exists as a **liquid** at room temperature, but it can also be a **solid** (ice) when frozen or a **gas** (water vapor) when heated. \n- **Unique Properties**: \n  - **High Specific Heat**: It absorbs and releases heat slowly, helping regulate temperature in organisms and the environment.\n  - **Cohesion & Adhesion**: Molecules stick to each other (cohesion) and to other surfaces (adhesion), enabling processes like capillary action in plants.\n  - **Solvent Ability**: Often called the \"universal solvent,\" it dissolves many substances, facilitating chemical reactions in living systems.\n\n### **Biological Importance**\n- **Life-Sustaining**: All known forms of life require water. It acts as a **medium for biochemical reactions**, transports nutrients, and helps remove waste.\n- **Body Function**: In humans, water makes up ~60% of the body, aiding in temperature regulation, digestion, and maintaining cell structure.\n\n### **Environmental Role**\n- **Hydrological Cycle**: Water cycles through evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and runoff, distributing fresh water across the planet.\n- **Ecosystems**: It shapes landscapes through erosion, forms habitats for aquatic life, and supports agriculture and weather patterns.\n\n### **Other Key Traits**\n- **Colorless, Odorless, and Tasteless**: Pure water has no color, smell, or taste, though it can appear blue in large quantities due to light absorption.\n- **Abundance**: Covers ~71% of Earth's surface, though only ~2.5% is freshwater, with most locked in ice or underground.\n\nIn summary, water is a simple yet extraordinary molecule whose unique properties make it indispensable for life, environmental stability, and countless natural and industrial processes."
